# Quill, on the Marrow's rail; then the pier at dawn.
dialogue quill4
  node farewell quill "Yellow flag on the boom, cargo. Nobody leaves the Marrow. Except customs. That's a regulation. You're a clerk again."
    -> farewell2
  node farewell2 quill "If she's still here at the dawn bell, Cray writes her down as a plague ship. Then the guns practise. We sail at dawn either way."
    note dawn_bell "Cray has the Marrow under a yellow flag. If she's still at anchor at the dawn bell, he writes her down as a plague ship. She sails at dawn either way."
    > "Then I have until dawn." -> until
      add aff 1
    > "I've a berth and a ship now. Dawn's a long way off." -> ages
    > "Come ashore. I'll write you a pass." -> pass
  node ages quill "That was the easy night, cargo. Nobody was trying to drown you on paper."
    -> until
  node pass quill "Signed by who? There's a lamp in Bramwick's window, and it isn't Bramwick. He's up there writing."
    -> until
  node until quill "You have until dawn."
    -> beat
  node beat narrator "She looks at me a moment longer than the harbour needs."
    -> name
  node name quill "Fenn."
    -> noticed
  node noticed narrator "It's the first time she has said it. She sees me notice. I see her see me notice. She glares at the lighthouse as if it started it."
    set farewell
    -> late
  node late quill "Don't be late."
    > "I'm never late. I'm a civil servant." -> civil
      add aff 1
    > "Say it again." -> again
      add aff 1
    > "(Nod, and go.)" -> END
  node civil quill "You're never early either. I've noticed. Go."
  node again quill "No. It's rationed. …Go on. The dawn isn't getting any later."
  # Talking up to the rail afterwards.
  node rail quill "Still here, cargo? The bell won't wait because you look worried. I've asked bells. They don't."
    > "We did it. Cray's finished." if inquiry_done -> done
    > "How's my father?" if not seen:quill4.dad -> dad
    > "How do I beat a man who writes everything down?" if not inquiry_done -> plan
    > "Show me the Liar again." if night_watch and not seen:quill4.liar -> liar
      add aff 1
    > "I'll be back before dawn." -> back
  node done quill "I heard. The whole harbour heard. Hobb cried on the capstan. Now get that flag off the boom. I want solid ground."
  node dad quill "Up and down the rail. He's moved flag sixteen to the masthead. Vane let him. She never lets anyone do anything."
    -> crates
  node crates quill "Vane found out what was in her crates. She's been quiet. Hobb hid the cargo book, in case she throws it at him."
  node plan quill "You're asking the navigator? Good. He lies on paper. Check every page he wrote. See where they cross. Start with Bramwick."
  node liar quill "There. Low over the lighthouse. It's moved since I showed you. It always moves. I like that. Go and be a clerk at somebody."
  node back quill "I know. I'm counting on it. I'm also counting the bells, so don't test me."
  # On the pier, once the quarantine's lifted and before the ledger's put right.
  node pier quill "Solid ground. I hate it. It just sits there. The book, cargo. Fix it, take it up the steps, then find me."
    > "You came ashore." -> ashore
    > "On my way." -> END
  node ashore quill "Vane said stretch my legs. I've stretched them as far as this bollard. It's a good bollard. I'm keeping it."
  # Dawn, on the pier: the bell, the margin, then the choice.
  node bell narrator "Up the hill, the dawn bell rings. Nobody in Port Vela writes anything down."
    -> margin
  node margin narrator "I take out the harbour ledger. There's a margin down every page. In three years I've never used it. Clerks aren't encouraged to."
    -> margin2
  node margin2 narrator "I write the ships first. Six lines, in the proper column. Then the margin, in pencil. Ink is for the record. This is for me."
    -> names
  # The margin is the only page in the book nobody makes him write. Each name is a choice
  # so it can wait on a real flag (dialogue nodes have no conditions of their own).
  node names narrator "The pencil's shorter than I remember. The margin's longer."
    > "(Vane. She asked for a ledger.)" if seen:vane4.page and not margin_vane -> margin_vane
    > "(Nell. She wanted it written down.)" if seen:nell.wheel4 and not margin_nell -> margin_nell
    > "(Old Onn. Not the harbourmaster.)" if (seen:onn.promise or seen:onn.home) and not margin_onn -> margin_onn
    > "(Marta. Who said not to write it.)" if seen:bramwick4.onions and not margin_marta -> margin_marta
    > "(Bramwick. Who wrote my father down.)" if (seen:bramwick.confess3 or seen:bramwick4.entry) and not margin_bram -> margin_bram
    > "(Turn to the back page.)" -> pike
  node margin_vane narrator "VANE. CLAIM REFUSED ON A TECHNICALITY. I write it under Cray's six, small, in pencil. It isn't a claim now. It's a correction."
    set margin_vane
    -> names
  node margin_nell narrator "NELL, UPPER TOWN, SAID SO FIRST. She wanted it in a ledger. This is the only one I have."
    set margin_nell
    -> names
  node margin_onn narrator "TEN OFF THIS STREET. TWELVE FROM DOWN THE HILL. COUNTED BACK. She asked for the clerk, not the harbourmaster. She gets the clerk."
    set margin_onn
    -> names
  node margin_marta narrator "NOTHING HAPPENED IN THE SALTY KEEL. Under it, smaller: EVERYTHING DID."
    set margin_marta
    -> names
  node margin_bram narrator "BRAMWICK. WROTE MY FATHER DOWN AND NEVER ONCE BELIEVED IT. Under it, smaller: HE WAS WRONG."
    set margin_bram
    -> names
  node pike narrator "Then I copy Pike's roll into the back. A hundred and thirty names. I get four wrong. Pike would have got none wrong. I leave them in."
    -> caught
  node caught quill "What are you doing?"
    -> correct
  node correct fenn "Correcting the record."
    -> atdawn
  node atdawn quill "At dawn. With a bell going."
    -> onlygood
  node onlygood fenn "It's the only thing I'm good at."
    -> whyask
  node whyask quill "I know. It's why I'm asking."
    -> dawn
  node dawn narrator "The sky over the headland is the colour of weak tea. Quill sits on her bollard, one bare foot over the water, waiting as if she isn't."
    -> sea
  node sea quill "Well, cargo. Sea or desk? You found your father last night. The whole harbour's heard Bramwick offer you a desk."
    -> tide
  node tide quill "The tide doesn't care. I do. Don't tell the tide."
    > "You called me Fenn. Earlier." if not seen:quill4.once -> once
    > "Sign me on as purser. The stars are yours." -> purser
    > "I'll keep the ledger honest. Come back every season?" -> season
    > "Upper Town first. I owe somebody up there an ending." if not seen:onn.home -> upfirst
  node once quill "Once. It's rationed. I'm saving the rest for when you've earned them."
    -> sea2
  node sea2 quill "So. Sea or desk? Take your time. Not that much."
    > "Sign me on as purser. The stars are yours." -> purser
    > "I'll keep the ledger honest. Come back every season?" -> season
    > "Upper Town first. I owe somebody up there an ending." if not seen:onn.home -> upfirst
  node upfirst quill "Upper Town first, cargo. Go on. I was a lookout for years. Waiting's the job."
  node purser narrator "She tries very hard not to smile, and loses by a distance."
    -> biscuits
  node biscuits quill "Purser. Vane will make you count the biscuits."
    > "Then I'll count them beautifully." -> aboard
    > "(Kiss her.)" if aff >= 14 -> pkiss
  node pkiss narrator "I kiss her on the pier, in front of the customs house, the lighthouse, and my father, who has found a rope to coil very slowly."
    -> logging
  node logging ansel "Don't mind me. I'm logging it."
    -> ptwo
  node ptwo quill "Get aboard, then. …Fenn. That's two. Don't get used to it."
    > "(Go aboard.)" -> END
      set ending_pirate
      act 4
  node aboard quill "Get aboard, then, cargo. The tide's turning. So, apparently, are you."
    > "(Go aboard.)" -> END
      set ending_pirate
      act 4
  node season narrator "She looks at the customs house for a long moment, and then back at me."
    -> every
  node every quill "Every season. I'll bring you a new star each time. You can write it down."
    > "I'll underline it." -> quay
      add aff 1
    > "I'll stamp it." -> quay
    > "(Kiss her.)" if aff >= 14 -> dkiss
  node dkiss narrator "I kiss her. Behind us the customs-house window bangs open. Bramwick starts “Regulation—”. Marta says “Shut that window.” He does. Slowly."
    -> dtwo
  node dtwo quill "Be on the quay when we come in, Fenn. That's two. I'll want a receipt."
    > "(Watch her go.)" -> END
      set ending_desk
      act 4
  node quay quill "Be on the quay when we come in. Don't be late."
    > "(Watch her go.)" -> END
      set ending_desk
      act 4
